{
  "summary": "Adds a `ReconstructMultipath` method to the `Descriptor` interface to invert descriptor multipath expansions. Given a base expanded descriptor and its remaining expansion siblings, it reconstructs the original multipath descriptor object. It also adds unit, invalid-case, and fuzz tests verifying expansion and reconstruction round-tripping.",
  "problem": "Multipath descriptors expand into multiple single-path descriptors, but there is no mechanism to reverse this expansion and recover the unified multipath descriptor from its individual expanded components.",
  "evidence": [
   "PR description: \"GetMultipathExpansion returns the multiple descriptors represented by a multipath descriptor. This expansion is reversible - given the expansion in the order of the multipath elements, it is possible to determine what the original multipath descriptor was. This PR adds ReconstructMultipath to produce a new Descriptor representing the multipath descriptor that produced the expansion.\"",
   "Commit 2cda830d1b implements ReconstructMultipath and subsequent commits add roundtrip, invalid case, and fuzz test coverage."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36442"
    ],
    "enables": [
      "#36444"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Part of a PR stack on multipath descriptors. It builds on #36442, which refactors `Parse` to return a single `Descriptor` and represents multipath descriptors directly.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Adds ReconstructMultipath to rebuild a single multipath descriptor object from an ordered set of its expanded single-path descriptors. This makes descriptor multipath expansion reversible in memory for descriptor-aware wallet and tooling workflows. It includes fuzzing and extensive unit tests for round-tripping and invalid inputs. Depends on #36442 and is required by #36444.",
